msgid "Do not use display:none, embed an API key, or reuse another recipient's tracking URL. A plain-text-only email cannot load this image. This plugin does not send emails or track clicks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:45
msgid "5. Retrieve Requests"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:47
msgid "Add <code>external_id</code> to filter one message, and <code>from</code>/<code>to</code> for inclusive UTC date boundaries such as <code>2026-10-30T00:00:00Z</code>. Page starts at 1; per_page is 1-100. Results are newest first; use event IDs to reconcile duplicates when new requests arrive during pagination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:49
msgid "Responses include request count, first/latest request timestamps in UTC, and (for events) the paginated event list. The total is the number of pixel requests, not the number of distinct readers. Dates are serialized as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ. Invalid IDs, dates, and pagination return 400; invalid keys or scope return 401; production HTTP returns 403; storage failures return 500."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:50
msgid "The WordPress Events tab uses the site date format, time format, and timezone from Settings > General. Its date filters use the site timezone, and its paginated table offers 10, 25, 50, or 100 events per page. API timestamps and API date filters remain UTC."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:51
msgid "Omit external_id to retrieve events for the whole project. Events are paginated, with at most 100 per response; fetch all pages using X-WP-TotalPages. The summary endpoint returns the matching count and first/latest timestamps in one response, not a full export of messages or project settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:52
msgid "Use last_days=5 on events or summary for the preceding five times 24 hours in UTC, ending at request time. Values must be whole numbers from 1 to 36500. It works for the whole project or with external_id. Do not combine last_days with from or to; that returns HTTP 400. Project retention still applies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:55
msgid "Time-filtered responses include date_range.from and date_range.to as ISO UTC timestamps. For consistent pagination, reuse those resolved values as from and to on subsequent pages and omit last_days. Otherwise the relative time window is recalculated on each request. Date boundaries are inclusive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:56
msgid "6. Retention and Reliability"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:57
msgid "Each project defaults to indefinite event history. Optional rolling 90-day retention hides expired events immediately and deletes them through hourly WordPress scheduled cleanup. Message IDs and links remain valid indefinitely, so an email opened years later can record another request. Switching back to indefinite cannot restore deleted events."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:58
msgid "WP-Cron depends on site traffic. For strict physical deletion deadlines, configure server cron to run <code>wp cron event run --due-now</code>. Backups and external logs need their own retention policies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:59
msgid "Exclude every request with the <code>wtp_pixel</code> query parameter from CDN, reverse-proxy, and WordPress page caches. Exclude authenticated API routes from caching too. If your server strips Authorization headers, configure it to forward them to PHP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:60
msgid "Every received valid GET is recorded, including repeat requests. HEAD requests are not recorded. Apple Mail Privacy Protection, image proxies, security scanners, disabled images, and email-client caching can create or suppress requests. These events cannot prove that a person read an email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:61
msgid "7. Privacy and Updates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:62
msgid "The plugin stores external IDs and request timestamps, not recipient addresses, IP addresses, user agents, or tracking cookies. Pseudonymous tracking can still be subject to privacy law and consent requirements. Server/CDN logs may collect additional data independently."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:63
msgid "Stable GitHub Releases appear through WordPress's normal update checks. Detection is periodic, not immediate; automatic installation depends on your site's automatic-update settings. No separate updater plugin or GitHub token is required for public releases."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:64
msgid "Deactivating or uninstalling the plugin preserves its data. Deleting a project explicitly in admin permanently deletes its keys, messages, and events."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:65
msgid "8. Test Your Live API"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:66
msgid "The optional command-line tester requires Node.js 22 or newer and a project API key. Run it only against a site and project you are authorized to test. Download the generic script and run the commands below from its directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:67
msgid "Download live API tester"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:68
msgid "Enter the API namespace URL when prompted, then the project ID and API key. The key prompt is hidden. Configuration stays in environment variables; never save live credentials, site details, or response data in project files or shared commands."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:71
msgid "The default is read-only: it checks authentication and summary retrieval without creating data. The tester prints only check results, not API keys, message IDs, tracking URLs, or raw responses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:72
msgid "For a dedicated test project, the optional write test creates two messages and two pixel events. It checks registration, repeated pixel requests, pagination, and summaries. Those records remain in the project for inspection; the tester does not delete projects or revoke keys."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tutorial.php:74
msgid "Revoke disposable API keys after testing. HTTPS is required; redirects are not followed and credentials are never forwarded to another origin. Hosting logs have their own retention policies."
msgstr ""
